# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A DENYLIST: ignore everything, then name what the image needs.
#
#  The usual .dockerignore lists what to leave out — node_modules, .git, .env. That
#  shape fails open: every new sensitive file needs someone to remember a new rule,
#  and the day they forget, `COPY . .` bakes it into an image layer. Layers are
#  shipped to registries and pulled onto every host, and deleting the file in a
#  later layer does not remove it from the earlier one. This repo already has two
#  files of exactly that kind (.env, *.local.md), and .gitignore needed a bug fix
#  before it covered the first one correctly.
#
#  An allowlist fails closed. Forget to list a new source directory and the
#  container dies at startup with MODULE_NOT_FOUND — loud, immediate, caught by the
#  CI container job. Forget a rule in a denylist and nothing fails at all.
#
#  What is deliberately left out by omission: tests, lint/format config, docs,
#  .git, and node_modules (the image installs its own, from the lockfile, for
#  Linux — a host node_modules may hold binaries built for a different OS).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

*

!package.json
!package-lock.json

!app.js
!server.js
!config
!db
!middleware
!repositories
!routes
!services
!utils
